# Rows to merge into docs/TECH-DEBT.md

Source: `docs/audits/tech-debt/fix-roomtimeline/` (job `fixrt`, 2026-11-12), three behavior fixes on `HEAD` `5deb37fd5`, approved in `docs/REMOVE-TECHNICAL-DEBT-PLAN.md` Key Decisions. Evidence and runs: `README.md` and `checks.raw.log` in that folder.

## Debt Ledger: status updates

| Item | New status |
|---|---|
| RT-10 | fixed in `01-day-separators-in-chat-locale.patch`: `dayLabel` formats an older day with the chat's locale (`get(locale)` from `i18n-svelte`, as `ProximityChatRoom.ts` does for `Intl.ListFormat`). The pin from `4ab34f19d` flips: with the chat in French on an en-US runtime the labels read "ven. 2 janv.", "Hier", "Aujourd'hui" (on `HEAD`: "Fri, Jan 2", "Hier", "Aujourd'hui"). A locale change while the room is open still waits for the next timeline change (RT-05, not fixed). |
| RT-09 | fixed in `02-replay-focus-highlight.patch`: `scrollToTimelineEvent` adds `highlight-message` with an `animationend` listener on the row that removes the class, and itself, when the row's own animation ends (an animation ending inside the message is ignored), so the next focus adds the class again. Pinned by "RT-09 (fixed): ends the highlight when its pulse ends, so focusing the same message again plays it again" (jsdom: the test dispatches `animationend`). A browser check of the replayed pulse stays open. The row no longer keeps the class's 10% background after the pulse (inferred from the CSS, not seen in a browser). |
| RT-02 | fixed in `03-mark-read-only-at-bottom.patch`: the receipt effect also requires `autoScroll`, so the room is marked read only while the timeline is pinned at the bottom and the tab is visible; getting back to the bottom, with the jump button or by scrolling, marks it read as the button's count clears. The pin from `30b3a76b8` flips (the 2 messages counted as new are not reported read); the hidden-tab behavior stays pinned; the new test "RT-02 (fixed): marks the room read when the user gets back to the bottom, with the jump button or by scrolling" covers the return. Two cases remain: RT-11 and RT-12. |

## Debt Ledger: new rows

| Item | Location | Type | Risk | Effort | Priority | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| RT-11: a room that opens away from the bottom is still marked read at open. The receipt effect runs as soon as the room is ready and has a last row, while `autoScroll` still holds its initial `true`; the open then un-pins the list to show the "New messages" line (`scrollToFirstUnread`) or a focused message (`scrollToTimelineEvent`). The unread messages below the line, or below the focused message, are reported read before the user has seen them. | `RoomTimeline.svelte` (after patch 3) the receipt effect `:411-415`, `scrollToFirstUnread` `:378-391`, `focusPendingTimelineRequestOrScrollToBottom` `:362-375`, `scrollToTimelineEvent` `:656-689` | quirk (the RT-02 decision does not hold at open) | low to medium (the same over-claiming receipt as RT-02, once per open with more unread messages than one screen, or with a focus request) | S (hold the receipt until the open has chosen where to scroll; the order of Svelte's effect flush and the open's promise chain matters, see the README) | P3 | open; shown by a probe run, not pinned: on stage 3, both "opens on the New messages line" and "a focus request pending at open" call `setTimelineAsRead` once at open (`probe.diff`, `checks.raw.log` section `f-probe`) |
| RT-12: since RT-02's fix, each return to the bottom calls `setTimelineAsRead`, also when nothing arrived since the last receipt. `MatrixChatRoom.setTimelineAsRead` always posts a receipt for the last live event, and `matrix-js-sdk`'s `sendReceipt` does not skip one it already sent (`node_modules/matrix-js-sdk/lib/client.js:2508-2530`), so a user who scrolls up and back sends one request and one local echo per return. | `RoomTimeline.svelte` (after patch 3) the receipt effect `:411-415`; `MatrixChatRoom.ts:1953-1964` | performance (one request per gesture) | low (inferred from the code; whether Synapse fans out a receipt for an already-read event was not checked) | S (skip the receipt when the last rendered row is the one last reported read, after checking that unread thread messages do not rely on the repeat) | P3 | open; not pinned |
